  "rationale": "The national split is not materially overstated. Indonesian \"ruang rapat\" and Malaysian \"bilik mesyuarat\" are distinct, ordinary workplace terms, while shared English \"meeting room\" is a valid cross-variety cue rather than an answer overlap. The sense and relation are aligned. No dedicated false-friend contrast is required: both Indonesian and Malaysian Malay also have meeting-related senses for \"rapat\", so the contrast would not be reliably exclusive.",
  "claim_reviews": [
    {
      "subject": "English cue and sense",
      "conclusion": "Correct and well aligned: \"meeting room\" means a room used for meetings, matching the supplied workplace sense.",
      "material_risk": false,
      "evidence_refs": [
        "https://dictionary.cambridge.org/us/dictionary/english/meeting-room"
      ]
    },
    {
      "subject": "Indonesian answer",
      "conclusion": "\"Ruang rapat\" is an ordinary Indonesian expression for a meeting room and is supported by Indonesian government usage and Indonesian terminology references.",
      "material_risk": false,
      "evidence_refs": [
        "https://badanbahasa.kemendikdasmen.go.id/berita-detail/3220/cetak-ulang-kbbi-edisi-kelima",
        "https://repositori.kemendikdasmen.go.id/4478/1/Bahasa%20dan%20Susastra%20Dalam%20Guntingan%20-%20Oktober%201995%20Nomor%20122.pdf"
      ]
    },
    {
      "subject": "Malaysian answer",
      "conclusion": "\"Bilik mesyuarat\" is an ordinary Malaysian Malay term for a meeting room, attested in official Malaysian government facilities and terminology usage.",
      "material_risk": false,
      "evidence_refs": [
        "https://ppk.ppj.gov.my/bilik-mesyuarat",
        "https://www.planmalaysia.gov.my/main/article/sistem-tempahan-bilik-planmalaysia",
        "https://prpm.dbp.gov.my/Cari1?d=123312&keyword=mesyuarat"
      ]
    },
    {
      "subject": "National split and final relation",
      "conclusion": "The answers are materially different common workplace terms, so \"different-common-word\" is justified. The shared English cue does not constitute answer-form overlap, and no evidence shows that either localized form is the ordinary default of the other variety.",
      "material_risk": false,
      "evidence_refs": [
        "https://badanbahasa.kemendikdasmen.go.id/berita-detail/3220/cetak-ulang-kbbi-edisi-kelima",
        "https://ppk.ppj.gov.my/bilik-mesyuarat",
        "https://prpm.dbp.gov.my/Cari1?d=123312&keyword=mesyuarat"
      ]
    },
    {
      "subject": "False-friend contrast",
      "conclusion": "No material false-friend contrast is required. Indonesian KBBI gives \"rapat\" the meeting sense, while Malaysian PRPM also records \"rapat\" as a meeting or assembly, alongside its proximity-related sense; therefore presenting the forms as a strict false-friend contrast would be misleading.",
      "material_risk": false,
      "evidence_refs": [
        "https://kbbi.web.id/rapat-2.html",
        "https://prpm.dbp.gov.my/Cari1?d=73980&keyword=rapat%20II"
      ]
    }
  ]
